{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/992284-npc-generation","id":992284,"title":"NPC Generation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-23T23:47:04-07:00","id":992284,"title":"NPC Generation","content":"I'm sorry if this has been touched upon before, but I've always been bad at forum search engines.<br /> <br /> I'm planning on running a Vampire game for the first time, and I've been having some trouble deciding how dangerous certain of the big city players should be. I found a quick generation guide for building dice pools for Beginners, Competents, Veterans, Experts, and Masters, but I think that would be better for on the fly creation and full sheets should flesh out the big guys. I'm either missing this in the VTR 2e book completely, or it doesn't really discuss it beyond the Experienced Kindred table in the creation quick guide.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any tips? My thought so far was to generate them using the Experienced Kindred table on page 82 and giving the NPCs a sheet like any other character, plus 1 BP per rank up in the table (ex: Urban Legend would be BP 7) and then the bonus experience listed there on top of the free BP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","name":"Ifisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-24T03:14:25-07:00","id":992310,"title":"","content":"I like building characters so I just use that table and go to town.<br /> <br /> I also handle the BP as a normal character, +1 for every 50 years. If I want them to have more BP I use their experience.<br /> <br /> Also also, I don\u00b4t use the number strictly, just a ballpark. If I reach a point I\u00b4m satisfied I stop spending, If I spend it all and am still not satisfied It helps to get the sense that the character is uncommonly powerful, but I keep spending.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T18:17:56-07:00","id":993209,"title":"","content":"My tips: don't bother too much with that yet. You don't need sheets for the big guys in the beginning, so let time decide what traits those characters need. NPCs like that shouldn't be defined by point-buy rules because their precise traits should be defined by chronicle's necessities.<br /> <br /> Then take note of the traits you want a given NPC to have <u>or lack</u>, and with time you'll have a clear picture of what the sheet should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T05:36:10-07:00","id":993448,"title":"","content":"In general 'balance' is comparative. Are they meant to be a hard fight? Give the character high health and a combat dice pool around the best party member's. In general this rule works for whatever type of character you are building. Pay attention to what the pool totals to, if it's 10 and the highest PC only has 6 it tells you they'll likely struggle in that situation (although the players' highest pools tells you the encounters they want to focus on).<br /> <br /> Now, onto full build stuff, the first thing to remember is notice what an NPC's pools are. In Vampire this will normally max out at about 12 (as it's hard to remain active at BP6+), but as before compare to the PC's pools. Blood Potency should be roughly (years active/50)+(1 to 3), and end up in the region of one to seven in general, although it'll sometimes reach 10. For disciplines just give them whatever you like, I have a formula I like as a guideline (sqrt(age/10)+3) but characters should vary from whatever guideline you pick wildly. For merits just give them any styles and retainers they need (as well as status dots), Allies/Contacts/Staff/special skills can really just be determined in-session as needed.<br /> <br /> EDIT: don't bother counting Experiences, if you're tracking the character's pools then you're just unfairly restricting Prince McLord if you don't have the Experiences to give him Presence 5 and Majesty 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":4507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","user":"TwoDSix","date":". 10-26-2016, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T09:15:32-07:00","id":993530,"title":"","content":"If someone has a little cheat sheet built up. I think that would be great if you want to share ^.^ <br /> <br /> <br /> In my games, I usually play to the clan stereotypes. If they are fighting a Gangrel, it usually has protean and resilience. A Daeva has Majesty and Celerity. Ect.<br /> <br /> However, I dont lay out every cop, gang member, bartender...ect that the group might pick a fight with. I usually have something like the average person has 2 dots in things. 3 is slightly above average, 4 is exceptional and 5 is well.. Amazing.<br /> <br /> So like the average Joe might have 2+2 to sneak up on the vampire, where as the ninja might have 4+4. The cop is likely going to be above average in perceptions, detecting lies, resolve checks. Ect. That's how I usually base things.<br /> <br /> If it's going to be a hard fight I usually go with 9 health, 10-12 dice pool for specialties and merits. Kind of go with averages instead of spending my time drawing up thousands of NPCs. Ones the players might never even encounter or encounter again. <br /> <br /> Though the important people, like the Prince or Primogens, I draw out and just give them what I think they should have without worrying about the exp cost. like TwoDsix said, you might end up unfairly restricting them. If you think your Daeva prince should have 5 presence and 5 majesty, give it to them. It's your city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-27T01:57:33-07:00","id":993940,"title":"","content":"My cheat sheet is: Decide on a BP of the character, based on age, diablerie, power growth speed/whatever.<br /> For each BP above one (since with one you're starting character), I give<br /> 2 attributes,<br /> 4 skills,<br /> 1 specialty, <br /> 2 disciplines (one of which must be in-clan)<br /> 1 Devotion (or a Blood Sorcery Theme, if applicable)<br /> 4 to 8 merit dots (i keep this one more flexible, as some high social standing people will need a lot more merits in allies and shit, where some are not)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}